## 16. Risk controls

| Risk | Control | Stop-ship condition |
|---|---|---|
| Current browser failures | M0 triage, M1 fixes, M2 review, M3 full rerun | Any unexplained failure remains. |
| False exact-commit claim | Candidate freeze and evidence manifest | Evidence SHA differs from release SHA. |
| Duplicate or conflicting financial movement | Idempotency, canonical fingerprints, locking, immutable postings | Any duplicate movement or unexplained conflict. |
| Stale balance shown as current | Version requirement, bounded wait, PostgreSQL fallback | Any stale-current result. |
| Cross-tenant disclosure | Server authorization and non-disclosing errors | Any unauthorized disclosure. |
| Misleading financial/delivery state | Separate state dimensions and approved copy | Any UI or API conflation that can cause unsafe action. |
| WebRTC data or command leakage | Ephemeral bounded channel, no commands/transcript, strict audits, TURN gate | Any persisted/logged signalling/chat or command path. |
| Migration incompatibility | Forward migration and compatibility suite | Any supported upgrade failure or history rewrite. |
| Unproven accessibility | Automated plus named physical/assistive review | Critical journey cannot be completed. |
| Unproven managed recovery | Provider PITR plus reconciliation | RPO/RTO or zero-mismatch evidence absent. |
| Missing legal/finance authority | Signed decisions before managed use | Required decision absent or expired. |

