## 18. Completion checklist

- [ ] Every PRD required feature maps to an owner, implementation location, and passing proof.
- [ ] All 52 current Playwright failures are resolved and the complete suite passes.
- [ ] Visual changes are individually reviewed; no blanket snapshot approval is used.
- [ ] Responsive, accessibility, physical-device, and moderated-usability evidence is complete.
- [ ] Full frontend, Go, security, migration, container, performance, artifact, real-stack, fault, and recovery gates pass.
- [ ] Exact-commit local-MVP evidence is published and approved.
- [ ] Active API-first, operator IA, and design/accessibility milestones are completed and requalified.
- [ ] Managed environment is not created before owners, budget, legal/finance decisions, and access are approved.
- [ ] Pilot traffic is not started before managed identity, security, observability, operations, and recovery gates pass.
- [ ] Production is not released without a signed evidence-based go/no-go decision.
- [ ] Optional public-site and payout tracks remain separate and gated.

## 19. Immediate next actions

1. Product owner sets `D0` and assigns the M0 owner table.
2. Release owner freezes the candidate SHA and publishes the 52-failure triage register.
3. Frontend/QA begin M1 in the order: account commands, onboarding/orientation, reconciliation, search, session, pagination.
4. Finance owner resolves any behavior/copy question before implementation changes financial meaning.
5. Product, engineering, and QA schedule the M2 device, accessibility, and moderated-review resources before M1 ends.

